%% title: Session Lifecycle — Customer Request & Onboarding State
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> UNAUTHENTICATED : app opens / token absent

    UNAUTHENTICATED --> ONBOARDING_ANONYMOUS : POST /onboarding/start\n(OnboardingResource, @PermitAll)
    ONBOARDING_ANONYMOUS --> PENDING_ACTIVATION : party created in party-service\n(kycStatus=PENDING_ACTIVATION)
    PENDING_ACTIVATION --> KYC_ACTIVE : operator completes KYC\n(out-of-band, admin-UI)
    KYC_ACTIVE --> AUTHENTICATED : customer obtains JWT\nfrom Keycloak customers realm

    UNAUTHENTICATED --> JWT_PRESENTED : app sends Bearer token
    JWT_PRESENTED --> JWT_INVALID : OIDC validation fails\n(wrong issuer / expired / bad sig)
    JWT_INVALID --> [*] : 401 Unauthorized

    JWT_PRESENTED --> AUTHENTICATED : JWT valid, CustomerIdentity resolved\n(party_id / sub extracted)

    AUTHENTICATED --> OWNERSHIP_CHECK : request targets\naccount / balance / tx / statement / payment
    OWNERSHIP_CHECK --> FORBIDDEN : account.partyId ≠ JWT partyId
    FORBIDDEN --> [*] : 403 Forbidden

    OWNERSHIP_CHECK --> M2M_TOKEN_RESOLVED : ownership confirmed
    AUTHENTICATED --> M2M_TOKEN_RESOLVED : party-scoped route\n(profile / notifications / devices / SCA)

    M2M_TOKEN_RESOLVED --> TOKEN_CACHE_HIT : cached token valid\n(>60 s remaining)
    M2M_TOKEN_RESOLVED --> TOKEN_REFRESH : token absent\nor <60 s to expiry
    TOKEN_REFRESH --> TOKEN_CACHE_HIT : Keycloak client_credentials\n(operator realm) → new token cached

    TOKEN_CACHE_HIT --> PROXYING : outbound request dispatched\nAuthorization: Bearer M2M token\nX-Customer-Party-Id: partyId

    PROXYING --> RESPONSE_OK : upstream 2xx / 4xx
    PROXYING --> TRANSPORT_ERROR : connect timeout / network failure

    RESPONSE_OK --> [*] : proxied response to app
    TRANSPORT_ERROR --> [*] : 502 {"error":"upstream unavailable"}

    PENDING_ACTIVATION --> KYC_GATE_BLOCKED : POST /onboarding/account\nbefore kycStatus=ACTIVE
    KYC_GATE_BLOCKED --> [*] : 403 Forbidden (ADR-0069)
